      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the angle of attack becomes too steep, the smooth airflow can no longer follow the wing's surface, causing the boundary layer to separate from the top of the wing and creating a turbulent wake. This separation drastically reduces the pressure difference between the top and bottom, effectively causing a sudden loss of lift known as a stall. Once stalled, the air is no longer being efficiently deflected downward by the wing, so the reaction force required to keep the plane flying disappears.",
